.TH DANBY-CHAOSDYNAMICS 1
.SH NAME
danby-chaosdynamics \- measure sensitive dependence in a dynamical system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/chaosdynamics
.SH DESCRIPTION
This experiment integrates an initial state and a perturbation separated by
10^-6 using identical deterministic Lorenz equations.  The lower trace is
log10 of Euclidean separation.  Its approximately linear growth intervals
correspond to exponential separation; their slope estimates a finite-time
Lyapunov exponent.  Folding and boundedness in the phase portrait prevent the
growth from continuing indefinitely.
.PP
Changing rho exposes non-chaotic and chaotic parameter regimes and separates
complicated geometry from measured sensitive dependence.
.SH SEE ALSO
danby-chaosintro(1), danby-chaos(1), numerics(2), plot(2)
